for the second time in four months an  attempt to remove pedro castillo from  office ends in failure the president  saying the impeachment trial was  baseless  everyone knows that it does not contain  a single element that sustains it we  only find words in the motion that have  no corroboration there's speculation  imaginary connections that don't support  facts and the law  in his brief defense the president  denied involvement in graft allegations  but his opponents say otherwise  the corruption that many defend grant  his accomplices millionaire bids the  prosecution says he has been involved in  influence peddling  analysts say the 20-part impeachment  motion was weak the corruption  allegations are still under  investigation by prosecutors  it has yet to be proven there has been  no evidence we deserve respect  the session was marked by interruptions  and insults and was briefly suspended  outside hundreds of riot police stopped  protesters from getting close castillo's  supporters said he must be allowed to  govern  he was democratically elected and must  be respected it's a legitimate  government those diliquants are trying  to oust him  short eight month long government has  been mired in controversy a poll found  fifty percent of peruvians want him gone  castillo is the fifth president in the  last six years it's no wonder peruvians  are fed up with pedo's political class  castillo has said he has made mistakes  but peruvians are increasingly  frustrated and many say they don't want  to wait for castillo to correct his  mistakes  he's a delinquent castillo has no morals  he has light he doesn't run a good  government he is a shame  the session lasted more than eight hours  but the impeachment had lost steam  before it started opponents were unable  to get castillo's allies to flip their  votes  now castillo says it's time to turn the  page but if not now opponents say they  will find a way to remove him from  office mariana sanchez lima peru
 

